WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:10.600
Friday. Yoga opens his inbox and finds a job offer. His first.

2
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:17.500
He is about to accept. Not because it fits, but because it came first.

3
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.800
One question stops him. Whose script is this line from?

4
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:30.900
Without a design, three scripts compete to run a career. The inheritance script: what the family respects.

5
00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:35.400
The feed script: whatever is trending this year.

6
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:39.900
And the first-offer script: whoever says yes first.

7
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:44.800
None of them is malicious. They are just unauthored.

8
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:50.500
So he designs first. His first mission sentence names a title.

9
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.200
A title is not a direction.

10
00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:00.700
The rewrite names a contribution: I help small businesses understand their own numbers.

11
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:09.200
A mission is a compass. It needs a first landmark: one outcome, three years out, with four parts.

12
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.200
A domain.

13
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:15.200
A level.

14
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.500
Evidence someone else can see.

15
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.600
And a line you refuse to cross.

16
00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:31.600
On Monday he answers the offer with two questions. Will I work with small clients? Who will I learn from?

17
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:40.100
He may still say yes. But now the yes is his: direction by design, not by first offer.

18
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:43.800
A mission names contribution, not titles.

19
00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:47.500
A 3-year outcome makes it plannable.

20
00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:56.000
Now it is your turn. For one big choice you face, ask: whose script is this line from?
